### REST Client / IntelliJ HTTP file. Variables are captured from responses with the `# @name` syntax.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@adminToken = local-admin-token
@idempotencyKey = http-file-{{$timestamp}}

### Create event
# @name createEvent
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Rock Night","date":"2035-06-01T20:00:00Z","venue":"Arena","capacity":50}

###
@eventId = {{createEvent.response.body.$.id}}

### List events
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events

### Availability
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/availability

### Availability stream (SSE, stays open)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/availability/stream
Accept: text/event-stream

### Purchase (202 Accepted)
# @name purchase
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{"eventId":"{{eventId}}","customerId":"customer-001","quantity":2}

###
@orderId = {{purchase.response.body.$.orderId}}

### Replay the same key (same orderId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: {{idempotencyKey}}

{"eventId":"{{eventId}}","customerId":"customer-001","quantity":2}

### Order status (repeat until PENDING_CONFIRMATION)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}

### Confirm
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{orderId}}/confirm

### Complimentary with admin token (201)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/complimentary
Content-Type: application/json
X-Admin-Token: {{adminToken}}

{"quantity":2}

### Complimentary without token (403)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/{{eventId}}/complimentary
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":1}

### Unknown event (404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/events/nope/availability

### Missing Idempotency-Key (400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{"eventId":"{{eventId}}","customerId":"customer-001","quantity":1}
